# ~/.bashrc.local.example — template for machine-local bash overrides.
#
# Copy to ~/.bashrc.local and edit. The generic .bashrc sources it at the TOP,
# before the non-interactive early-return, so PATH/toolchain changes here are
# visible to non-interactive bash too (VS Code Server, `ssh host cmd`).
#
#   cp Linux/.bashrc.local.example ~/.bashrc.local
#
# Not tracked by the repo (gitignored). Put machine-specific or non-public
# things here.

# --- Optional: hand off interactive bash to zsh -------------------------------
# Only needed on machines where you can't run `chsh -s $(command -v zsh)`.
# Normally leave this unset and let chsh make zsh your login shell.
# export DOTFILES_BASH_TO_ZSH=1

# --- Example: per-machine PATH / toolchains -----------------------------------
# export PATH="$HOME/.gobrew/current/bin:$HOME/.gobrew/bin:$PATH"
# export GOPATH="$HOME/.gobrew/current/go"

# --- Example: secrets sourced from a file outside the repo --------------------
# [ -f ~/.secrets.env ] && source ~/.secrets.env
